# steal — fail
#
# The steal verb attempted and missed: the checks pass, the dice do not, and the outcome block reports FAILURE.
#
# Reached in 12/12 of the sampled location ids (see --verb-probe). --location-type and
# --location-id decide the whole scene, so this does not depend on world generation; --npc-static
# pins people to one room; --observe-only pins the phase to one object, which is why the keyword is
# clicked by index (which word the prose highlights is not something a test can know).
#
# --organs arms=2: the rack's iron bar is heavy, and a free hand takes a heavy item only behind an
# arm of level 2 (PartyMember.HoldLimit). The seed's arms are weaker, which would refuse the pickup
# before the dice like a full pack; this script is about the verb, not the arm.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Room" --period dawn --observe-only "Test Chest" --organs arms=2

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

strategy fail-dice
goal steal
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
regions

click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180

expect FAILURE

# What makes this a steal test rather than an any-verb test: SUCCESS/FAILURE is the outcome banner
# of every verb alike, so only this can tell them apart.
expect-verb steal
# The failure assertion that means something: the verb's own consequence did NOT happen.
# Asserting the penalty instead would be flaky — FailurePenalties draws one entry of several,
# and only --penalty-only pins which (see cli/outcome/).
expect-no-outcome item_acquisition
quit
